{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass, etc.</b> From its profit they shall consecrate of it to HaShem." "<b>Not.</b> It shall be stored in a treasury, not in a place of wealth." "<b>For those who dwell before YHWH.</b> They are the exiles of Jerusalem, when they return in the days of Cyrus." "<b>To eat and be satisfied.</b> The exile shall be satisfied." "<b>And for covering.</b> A covering." "<b>Ancient.</b> Strong, like 'the thing has gone forth from your lips' (I Samuel 2:3)." "There are those who ask: does not the Torah forbid the hire of a harlot (Deuteronomy 23:19)? How then did the prophet say that the hire of the rock-harlot shall be holy? The answer: what is written in the Torah is the truth, and what the prophet said is by way of parable, and she is not a harlot at all."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:53.068305805Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}